# .claude/ is tracked selectively in this fork: CLAUDE.md and skills/ travel
# with the repo, everything else (local settings, session state) stays
# ignored. Must come after the blanket `.claude/*` and bare `CLAUDE.md`
# rules above — gitignore re-inclusion only wins over rules earlier in the
# file, and `CLAUDE.md` (no leading slash) would otherwise re-ignore
# .claude/CLAUDE.md too.
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

